{{!--
    reference/anchor-link - the link icon that makes something on a reference page
    addressable. Used once per operation (reference/operation) and once per property row
    (reference/schema-node), so the two stay identical rather than being kept in step by
    hand.

    A single element, with the icon mask on the anchor itself and the color and hover in
    the .ee-ref-anchor rule rather than a utility string: a tag page renders this up to 434
    times, where a wrapper span and a repeated 68-character class list cost real DOM nodes
    and parse time. The accessible name comes from aria-label, since there is no text.

    Params:
      target - the id to link to, without the "#" (required)
      label  - the full accessible name, e.g. "Link to this operation" (required)
      small  - true for the smaller icon used on property rows (optional)
      class  - extra classes on the anchor: the ms-auto that pushes the operation link to
               the end of its row, or the ee-ref-prop-anchor that keeps a property link
               hidden until its row is hovered (optional)
--}}
<a href="#{{target}}" class="ee-ref-anchor icon-[tabler--link] {{#if small}}size-3.5{{else}}size-4{{/if}}{{#if class}} {{class}}{{/if}}" aria-label="{{label}}"></a>
